 HISTORY                                                            46 1451
 -------                                                            46 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics    46 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The          46 1451
 inelastic scattering cross section libraries for O in BeO were     46 1451
 fully developed using ab-initio lattice dynamics (AILD) methods    46 1451
 [1]. BeO has a hexagonal wurtzite crystal structure with           46 1451
 symmetry belonging to the P6_3mc space group (#186). It was        46 1451
 modeled in VASP [2-4] using the GGA-PBE exchange-correlation       46 1451
 functional with a 450 eV plane wave energy cutoff and a 6x6x3      46 1451
 Monkhorst-Pack k-space mesh. The DOS was calculated in PHONON      46 1451
 [5] via the dynamical matrix method using a 4x4x2 supercell.       46 1451
 Eight temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law     46 1451
 Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to produce MT     46 1451
 = 2 (coherent) and MT = 4 data [6]. By convention, MAT=46 and      46 1451
 ZA=146 are used for O in BeO. This evaluation improves upon the    46 1451
 O_BeO evaluation in ENDF/B-VIII.0 by (1) updating the mass and     46 1451
 free atom cross section of O to be those of the                    46 1451
 naturally-weighted element and (2) using experimental lattice      46 1451
 parameters in the calculation of the coherent elastic (MT=2)       46 1451
 data [7-8]. The atomic masses and free atom cross sections were    46 1451
 taken from the ENDF/B-VIII.0 database [9], with the latter         46 1451
 corresponding to 1.0E-05 eV. The natural abundances of the O       46 1451
 isotopes were taken from the NIST database [10].                   46 1451
